Diffucore is an independent diffusion inference engine. It is not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or derived from any other diffusion UI or framework. Model
architectures and sampling algorithms are implemented from their original
research publications.

The fused Triton glue kernels (src/diffucore/models/_fused.py) and the INT8
Turing attention kernel (src/diffucore/kernels/int8_attn_sm75.cu) were created
by Dzakwan Haq (KayfaHaarukku, github.com/nawka12). Redistributions and
derivative works must retain this attribution.

The Krea 2 DiT (src/diffucore/models/krea2_dit.py) follows the architecture of
krea-ai/krea-2 (Apache License 2.0, Krea); its module names mirror
that implementation so released checkpoints load unchanged. Krea 2 weights are
not distributed with this product and carry their own license.

The MOSS-Image DiT (src/diffucore/models/moss_dit.py) and the sigma schedule in
src/diffucore/pipelines/_moss.py are ported from the reference
pipeline_moss_image.py of OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT (Apache License 2.0,
OpenMOSS Team); module names mirror it so released checkpoints load unchanged.
tests/_moss_reference.py is that reference code, vendored for the oracle tests.
MOSS-Image weights are not distributed with this product and carry their own
license.

The Qwen3.5 text encoder (src/diffucore/models/qwen35_text.py) follows the
Qwen3.5 text model in Hugging Face transformers (Apache License 2.0, The
Hugging Face Team and the Qwen Team); its parameter names mirror the released
checkpoints so they load unchanged.

This product bundles tokenizer vocabularies, each under the Apache License 2.0:
